Source: tt-bio-demo
Section: science
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tenstorrent <software@tenstorrent.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/tsingletaryTT/tt-bio-demo
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tt-bio-demo
Architecture: all
Depends:
 python3-gi,
 python3-gi-cairo,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
 python3-gemmi,
 libgl1,
 libglu1-mesa,
 curl,
 ca-certificates,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 gir1.2-webkit-6.0,
 tt-installer
Description: conference-booth demo -- protein folding on Tenstorrent hardware
 tt-bio-demo is a turnkey conference demo for tt-bio: protein structure
 prediction on Tenstorrent hardware. A visitor picks a protein and watches
 it condense out of noise into its folded structure in real time, computed
 on the Blackhole chips in the room.
 .
 This package ships the GTK4 UI, the compute-daemon source, the fold
 playlist and its input structures, and the systemd --user unit and desktop
 entry that launch the booth. It contains no Python runtime for tt-bio
 itself (see tt-bio-demo-runtime) and no model weights (see
 tt-bio-demo-weights) -- install tt-bio-demo-all for a complete booth.
 .
 gir1.2-webkit-6.0 is recommended, not required: it drives a small Tensix
 hardware-activity animation that the booth runs without if it is absent.

Package: tt-bio-demo-runtime
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 tt-bio-demo (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-venv,
 python3-pip,
 debconf | debconf-2.0,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Python runtime environments for tt-bio-demo
 Builds the two Python virtual environments tt-bio-demo needs under
 /opt/tt-bio-demo (one for the GTK4 UI, one for the tt-bio compute daemon)
 and pip-installs tt-bio pinned to a tested release tag.
 .
 Marked amd64 (not all) because what it actually installs -- a torch/ttnn
 wheel stack and the SFPI RISC-V cross-toolchain tt-bio's kernels need --
 only exists prebuilt for x86_64 hosts; there is nothing for this package
 to do on any other architecture.

Package: tt-bio-demo-weights
Architecture: all
Depends:
 tt-bio-demo (= ${binary:Version}),
 curl,
 ca-certificates,
 debconf | debconf-2.0,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: model weights for tt-bio-demo
 Downloads the OpenFold3 checkpoint and any other model weights the fold
 playlist needs, verifies their checksums, and pre-warms the tt-metal
 kernel cache so the first fold at the booth is already warm rather than
 paying a cold-compile cost in front of visitors.
 .
 Ships no weights itself: they are downloaded and verified in postinst, so
 this package is scripts and checksums only.

Package: tt-bio-demo-all
Architecture: all
Depends:
 tt-bio-demo (= ${binary:Version}),
 tt-bio-demo-runtime (= ${binary:Version}),
 tt-bio-demo-weights (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: tt-bio-demo, complete booth install (metapackage)
 Depends on tt-bio-demo, tt-bio-demo-runtime and tt-bio-demo-weights, so
 that `apt install tt-bio-demo-all` alone -- on a freshly imaged QB2 --
 produces a working conference booth. Carries no files of its own.
